WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.769
<v Ana Ribeiro>Good morning, Marina, Felipe. Thanks for making the time. Can you both hear me okay?</v>

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.800
<v Marina Lopes>Loud and clear. Sorry we're a couple of minutes late, the traffic on the highway this morning was a nightmare.</v>

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:18.000
<v Felipe Nunes>Same here. I left home at seven and I still barely made it.</v>

4
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:36.800
<v Ana Ribeiro>No problem at all, same for me, the usual Tuesday. So, the goal for today: you filled in our web form about a CRM, and I'd like to understand how your commercial team works today, what is not working, and whether Orbita is a good fit. Does that sound good?</v>

5
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:49.308
<v Marina Lopes>Perfect. Let me give you some context. Acme is a freight and warehousing company, we're about eight hundred and fifty people, and around a hundred of them are in the commercial area.</v>

6
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.231
<v Ana Ribeiro>And how does the commercial team manage customers and deals today?</v>

7
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:08.615
<v Felipe Nunes>Honestly, spreadsheets and Outlook. Each rep has their own spreadsheet of accounts, proposals live on a shared drive, and everything else is in people's inboxes.</v>

8
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:26.769
<v Felipe Nunes>When someone goes on holiday or leaves the company, we lose the history of the account. Last quarter we missed two contract renewals because nobody remembered the dates.</v>

9
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:51.615
<v Marina Lopes>And from my side, I have no visibility. Every Monday I ask for the pipeline and I get six different spreadsheets in six different formats. If this works, success for me is simple: zero missed renewals next year, and the Monday pipeline review done from one screen instead of six spreadsheets.</v>

10
00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:13.800
<v Ana Ribeiro>That's very common. Let me play it back to see if I got it right: you need one place where the whole team tracks accounts, deals and renewals, so nothing gets lost and you get a reliable view of the pipeline. Is that the need?</v>

11
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:23.615
<v Marina Lopes>Exactly. One place for every account and every deal, with renewal reminders, and a pipeline I can trust on Monday morning. That is the priority.</v>

12
00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:05.077
<v Ana Ribeiro>Who would use the system day to day?</v>

13
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:17.000
<v Felipe Nunes>The forty sales reps, our twelve account managers in customer success, and the leadership team, about eight managers, for the dashboards. So sixty users to start.</v>

14
00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:28.846
<v Ana Ribeiro>Sixty users, across sales, customer success and leadership. Got it.</v>

15
00:03:54.000 --> 00:04:02.462
<v Felipe Nunes>And the reps are on the road a lot, visiting warehouses and customers, so a mobile app is a must for them.</v>

16
00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:11.231
<v Ana Ribeiro>What else does the system need to do on day one?</v>

17
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:19.692
<v Felipe Nunes>Pipeline management, renewal alerts, email sync with Outlook so we stop copying emails by hand, and management dashboards for Marina.</v>

18
00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:37.800
<v Marina Lopes>By the way, Felipe, did you send the photos from Saturday's barbecue to the group? My husband keeps asking.</v>

19
00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:39.923
<v Felipe Nunes>Not yet, tonight. Sorry, Ana.</v>

20
00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:47.385
<v Ana Ribeiro>No worries. Now, about your systems: what would the CRM need to connect to?</v>

21
00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:58.769
<v Marina Lopes>Our transport management system, the TMS. It's ours, built in-house about ten years ago, and all the shipment data is there. We also use Orion ERP for invoicing.</v>

22
00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:22.769
<v Marina Lopes>And to be honest, that is my main worry. I am concerned about integrating with our in-house TMS. Anything that touches operations during peak season makes me nervous.</v>

23
00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:43.000
<v Felipe Nunes>My worry is adoption. We tried a sales tool three years ago and the reps hated it. They went back to their spreadsheets in two months.</v>

24
00:06:54.000 --> 00:07:09.000
<v Ana Ribeiro>Both are fair concerns. On the TMS, we did a similar integration with an in-house system for another logistics client last year. I will send you that reference case by Friday, so you can see how we handled it.</v>

25
00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:13.923
<v Marina Lopes>That would help a lot.</v>

26
00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:34.308
<v Ana Ribeiro>On adoption, we usually start from the reps' daily routine: the mobile app, the email sync, and nothing they have to type twice. We can go deeper on that in a workshop.</v>

27
00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:42.000
<v Ana Ribeiro>Can I ask about budget? Is there money set aside for this project?</v>

28
00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:51.308
<v Marina Lopes>Yes. We have between eighty and a hundred thousand dollars a year for the CRM, licences and support included.</v>

29
00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:15.846
<v Ana Ribeiro>That's helpful. Are you looking at other vendors as well?</v>

30
00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:24.538
<v Felipe Nunes>We had a first call with Northwind CRM, and we're getting a demo from PipeSpark next week.</v>

31
00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:32.462
<v Ana Ribeiro>Good to know, thanks for being open about it.</v>

32
00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:28.154
<v Felipe Nunes>Ana, unrelated question: is your team going to the logistics trade fair in Joinville this year?</v>

33
00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:31.308
<v Ana Ribeiro>Probably, our marketing team usually goes.</v>

34
00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:25.077
<v Ana Ribeiro>Who else would be involved in the decision?</v>

35
00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:39.923
<v Marina Lopes>I make the decision on this. It sits in my operations budget. But I will want our IT lead, Rui Tavares, to validate the technical side, the integration and the security.</v>

36
00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:54.231
<v Ana Ribeiro>And after Rui's validation, is there any other step? Procurement, legal?</v>

37
00:21:56.000 --> 00:22:00.615
<v Marina Lopes>Procurement needs three quotes for anything above fifty thousand. Then I sign.</v>

38
00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:13.923
<v Ana Ribeiro>And in terms of timing?</v>

39
00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:22.308
<v Marina Lopes>We need it live before our peak season starts in April, so go-live by March 2027 at the latest.</v>

40
00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:10.846
<v Felipe Nunes>One more thing for the reps: we need to see each customer's shipment status inside the CRM, otherwise they will keep calling operations.</v>

41
00:30:16.000 --> 00:30:21.769
<v Ana Ribeiro>That comes back to the TMS integration, so it's a good topic for the workshop.</v>

42
00:35:02.000 --> 00:35:14.692
<v Ana Ribeiro>Proposed next step: a technical scoping workshop with Rui, the week of 9 November, to look at the TMS data and the integration options. Pedro, our solutions engineer, would join from our side.</v>

43
00:35:19.000 --> 00:35:22.846
<v Marina Lopes>Yes, let's do that. I will make sure Rui joins.</v>

44
00:35:25.000 --> 00:35:30.385
<v Ana Ribeiro>Great. I will send the workshop invite together with the reference case by Friday.</v>

45
00:41:42.000 --> 00:41:49.800
<v Felipe Nunes>And Ana, if you have a short video of the mobile app, send it over. I'd like to show it to two of our senior reps.</v>

46
00:41:50.000 --> 00:41:52.692
<v Ana Ribeiro>Sure, I'll include it in Friday's email.</v>

47
00:42:12.000 --> 00:42:23.538
<v Felipe Nunes>For what it's worth, I'm the one who pushed for this project internally. If the mobile app is as good as it looks, I'll get the reps on board myself.</v>

48
00:42:40.000 --> 00:42:41.538
<v Marina Lopes>Thanks, Ana. Talk soon.</v>
